  "verdict": "At a properly converged C_P1 solution the released backward, our exact 6-DoF IFT and a branch-following FD all agree to 1.5% / 9.4% / 30% (cos 0.9999 / 0.9956 / 0.9661); our IFT alone matches the FD to 5e-6 / 2e-5 / 3e-4.  The published 1.37 / 1.31 / 0.92 was a basis error (released = d(rvec,t)/dtheta, published 'ift6' = omega): the same-pose basis factor alone is 1.37 / 1.26 / 0.76, and the published solutions were non-stationary (||grad C|| = 4e-3 / 3e-3 / 4e-4).  The remaining gap is the depth weighting (released differentiates sum_i S_i||e_i||^2, ours sum_i S_i^2||e_i||^2) plus the float32 implementation of the release, which loses accuracy as cond(f_y) grows (1.4e3 -> 9.1e4 here); it is case dependent, not a shared 6-DoF IFT."
 },
