 "verdicts": [
  "The released backward IS a correct IFT -- of its own implicit system f=0 (rel 1.6e-07 vs the exact IFT of f, 1.6e-07 vs central FD of the f-root forward).",
  "It is NOT the IFT of the algebraic LS solution (rel 1.68e-01 on the demo cube) nor of cv.solvePnP's geometric solution (17.1% on the toy), because f is the stationarity of the depth-weighted normalised reprojection cost sum_i S_i||e_i||^2, not of sum_i||r_i||^2.",
  "The P1 adaptation table in the published JSON is not reproducible from the committed script (P1ViaReleasedBPnP.forward raises TypeError; the in-tree p1_solve returns C=6.6e-02 vs the reported 1.6e-04 and feeds a permuted Jacobian to least_squares), and its FD reference is ~1000x larger than both gradient arms, i.e. invalid.",
  "The published rel_bpnp_vs_ift6 = 1.37/1.31/0.92 is dominated by a BASIS error: g_bpnp is d(rvec,t)/dtheta (parameter basis) while the published g_ift6 was the tangent (omega) rate; the same-vector basis factor is 0.76-1.37.",
